    keyPoints: ["input() always returns a string, even for pure numeric input - explicitly convert with int()/float() before doing arithmetic", "f-strings (f\"...{expression}...\") are the modern, idiomatic way to build formatted output in Python", "print()'s sep parameter controls the separator between multiple arguments; end controls what follows instead of the default newline"],
